{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-32033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-3y=0 \\\\ -3x+6y=2\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-32033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 6\\end{aligned}].$\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 6-(-3)\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-32033" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "53ad7294ab68a8da72a45b73d2d11026b24d6e022411f009ec40c3c1f268afa6"} {"question" "q-32033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-32033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{15}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & -3 \\\\ -3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-32033" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=-\\frac{1}{3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 3 \\\\ 3 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-102799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}3y=-x \\\\ 2y=1\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-102799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}x+3y=0 \\\\ 2y=1.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{1\\cdot 2-0\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-102799" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "53ad7294ab68a8da72a45b73d2d11026b24d6e022411f009ec40c3c1f268afa6"} {"question" "q-102799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-102799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=2[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{6}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-102799" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Which of the following represents the solution to the system of linear equations given below?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}5=2x-3y \\\\ 4x=y-2\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we reorganize the equations so that they are in the right order, to get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\begin{aligned}2x-3y=5 \\\\ 4x-y=-2.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can represent this system of equations in the form $Ax=b:$\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}].$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{2\\cdot (-1)-4\\cdot (-3)}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now find the solution to this system as:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "53ad7294ab68a8da72a45b73d2d11026b24d6e022411f009ec40c3c1f268afa6"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x=-\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ 4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -3 \\\\ -4 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] ["math" "x=\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}2 & -3 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-102806" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x=\\frac{1}{10}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-320797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The solution to the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x-6y=9 \\\\ 3y=-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\ncan be represented using matrix notation as\n\n| $x=$ {{field-1}} |\n| --- |\n\n| |  | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  | |  |  |  | |  | $9$ |  |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ |  | | . |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $3$ | {{field-2}} |  |  |  |\n|  | {{field-3}} | $4$ |  |  |  |\n|  | $9$ |  |  |  |  |\n|  | $-3$ |  |  |  |  |" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-320797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "This system can be written as\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTo find the solution, we need to calculate the inverse of the coefficient matrix \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -6 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nThis gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 3-0\\cdot (-6)}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can now represent the solution to this system as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & ={A}^{-1}b \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\begin{aligned}3 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 4\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-320797" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "53ad7294ab68a8da72a45b73d2d11026b24d6e022411f009ec40c3c1f268afa6"} {"question" "q-320797" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-320797" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{12}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36c41e"} {"question" "q-320797" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14014080/state.json" "file_sha256" "239c6f131425718e9730080a53ce04c8f469ce7edd38344c253c40dd8b36